# Local development only. Copy to .env.local (git-ignored) and fill it in. Never commit a real key.
#
# Gemini API key (from https://aistudio.google.com/apikey), read by BOTH local entry points:
#   npm run dev    -> the Vite dev server proxies /api/ai/gemini to Google and adds this key
#                     (the dev server listens on every network interface, so anyone on your LAN could
#                      reach that proxy while it runs; use it on a trusted network)
#   node server.js -> the same proxy, after checking the caller's Firebase sign-in and whitelist
# In production the key is NOT in this file and NOT in the JavaScript bundle: Cloud Run injects it from
# Secret Manager (secret "gemini-api-key") as the GEMINI_PROXY_KEY environment variable.
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# server.js has three more OPTIONAL runtime variables (README "server.js variables"):
# FIRESTORE_DATABASE_ID, VIALTRACK_API_KEY, GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS (needed for `node server.js` locally).
